---
import '../../styles/coordinate.css';
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { TrackerPreview } from '../../components/TrackerEditor';
---

<Layout
  title="Free Printables — Coordinate Grids & Habit Trackers | ChartsAI"
  description="Print coordinate grids, math activities and personalized habit trackers. Free A4 and Letter PDFs with live previews, no signup and no watermark."
>
  <section class="container listing-intro">
    <span class="eyebrow">A LITTLE MORE INTENTIONAL</span><h1>
      A useful page.<br /><em>Made for you.</em>
    </h1><p>
      Coordinate grids for your next lesson. Habit trackers for your next week. Customize a page or download a
      ready-made PDF.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="container section listing-cards">
    <article class="coordinate-feature">
      <p>
        <a href="/math-tools/">New: number lines, slope, transformations and quadratic worksheets ↗</a>
      </p><img
        src="/coordinate/assets/quadrants.svg"
        width="720"
        height="720"
        alt="Labelled points on a coordinate plane"
      /><span class="eyebrow">NEW · FOR LEARNING & TEACHING</span><h2>A grid. A question. An answer.</h2><p>
        Make a blank coordinate plane, plot your own points or create practice with a separate answer key.
        First or four quadrants, A4 or US Letter.
      </p><a class="button" href="/coordinate-plane-generator/">Make a coordinate plane ↗</a>
    </article>
    <div class="printable-feature">
      <div class="card-preview tracker-preview">
        <span class="card-index">YOUR NEXT LITTLE ROUTINE</span><div class="mini-paper">
          <TrackerPreview
            config={{
              title: 'Small steps, good days.',
              habits: ['Read a little', 'Move my body', 'Make something', 'Step outside', 'Wind down early'],
              month: '2026-09',
              period: 'week',
              paper: 'a4',
              ink: false,
            }}
          />
        </div>
      </div><div class="feature-copy">
        <span class="eyebrow">FREE · PERSONALIZABLE · READY TO PRINT</span><h2>
          Make room for<br />a good habit.
        </h2><p>
          Weekly or monthly. A4 or US Letter. Your habits, your title, and a little space to reflect. No
          account, email gate, or watermark.
        </p><a class="button" href="/printables/habit-tracker/">Make your habit tracker ↗</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container prose-section">
    <h2>A printable that fits your life</h2><p>
      A habit tracker is a simple sheet with a row for each habit and a box for each day. Mark a box when you
      complete the action. Choose weekly or monthly layouts, personal labels and an ink-friendly option. For
      math practice, the coordinate plane generator provides blank grids and labelled-point activities with
      answer keys.
    </p><p>
      Prefer to explore numbers you already have? Our <a href="/charts/">free chart makers</a> turn pasted values
      and spreadsheet data into downloadable charts.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="container section">
    <h2>Number line practice packs</h2><p>
      Print negative-number, fraction and unit-jump exercises with separate answer keys. <a
        href="/number-line-worksheets/">Download the free packs or generate 6–12 fresh questions →</a>
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>
